From a4986667d81e64108301a6dc70005996a7386f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 17:48:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/34] fix(systemd): harden gt-daemon unit against cgroup-kill
 failures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The gastown daemon spawns claude agents through tmux, which uses
systemd-run to place each pane in its own tmux-spawn-<uuid>.scope —
sibling to the gt-daemon.service cgroup, not child. With the default
KillMode=control-group, 'systemctl stop gt-daemon' tries to signal
every process in the service cgroup and intermittently fails the
eventual cgroup.kill with "Failed to kill control group: Invalid
argument", landing the unit in 'failed' state.

Incident (anvil, 2026-04-23 23:11:44): 'systemctl restart gt-daemon'
during the pre-push deploy timed out on stop, SIGKILL'd the daemon
but couldn't clean the cgroup, and the unit sat failed for 17h.
Subsequent restart attempts silently no-op'd on the failed unit,
which is why the deploy script logs 'Daemon restarted.' but the
binary in memory never swapped.

Fix: add KillMode=mixed + TimeoutStopSec=30s. Mixed mode sends SIGTERM
to the main gt process only (it drains its own bd children cleanly),
and only the cgroup.kill at timeout can tickle the EINVAL — which
for our usage pattern effectively never fires.

Applies to the embedded template; anvil's hand-rolled
gt-daemon.service was patched in place separately.
---
 internal/templates/systemd/gastown-daemon.service | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/internal/templates/systemd/gastown-daemon.service b/internal/templates/systemd/gastown-daemon.service
index b78a4492..1a9e5954 100644
--- a/internal/templates/systemd/gastown-daemon.service
+++ b/internal/templates/systemd/gastown-daemon.service
@@ -11,6 +11,15 @@ RestartSec=5s
 Environment="GT_TOWN_ROOT={{.TownRoot}}"
 StandardOutput=append:{{.TownRoot}}/daemon/daemon.log
 StandardError=append:{{.TownRoot}}/daemon/daemon.log
+# KillMode=mixed: SIGTERM the main gt process only, then SIGKILL the cgroup at
+# timeout. The daemon spawns claude agents via tmux-spawn-<uuid>.scope sibling
+# cgroups; with the default control-group KillMode, systemd tries to signal
+# every process in the service cgroup including transiently-adopted children,
+# which intermittently fails with "Failed to kill control group: Invalid
+# argument" and strands the unit in 'failed' state. Mixed mode lets the
+# daemon's own graceful shutdown drain its bd children cleanly.
+KillMode=mixed
+TimeoutStopSec=30s
 
 [Install]
 WantedBy=default.target
